WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.501
-An upcoming book reveals

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.670
shocking new details about the
Trump administration's

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.973
criminally negligent
COVID response

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.908
and Republicans blocked
a voting rights bill

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:12.211
as part of their ongoing attempt
to dismantle our democracy.

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.614
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:18.584
♪♪

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.853
As eager as we all are
to get back to normal,

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:23.323
we can't lose sight of the fact
that the COVID pandemic

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:24.691
is still very much with us.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.293
Vaccination rates in parts
of the country are lagging;

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.462
case numbers, in some states,
are rising;

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.465
a dangerous new variant is
driving up infections in the UK;

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:35.901
and models predict a possible
surge of cases in the fall.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.004
And, even as things
get better, overall,

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.805
there are still
constant reminders

00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:42.942
of how much our world has
changed in the last 16 months.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.645
Every time I reach across the
counter at my local coffee shop

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.614
to grab my iced oat latte
from the barista,

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:51.584
only to accidentally punch
the Plexiglas partition

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.553
that's still there to stop the
spread of contagious droplets

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:56.489
from a deadly disease,
I think to myself,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.090
"Oh, right, COVID."

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.860
Not that, I should note,
the glass does anything.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.361
I'm pretty sure aerosols

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:05.031
can find their way
around a glass partition.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:08.934
It's like trying to keep ants
out of your house with a sign.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:11.170
We're also constantly reminded,

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.106
even five months
after he left office,

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.707
that Trump's response
to the pandemic

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.944
was, somehow,
much worse and much crazier

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.345
than we even knew at the time.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.180
Every day, we keep hearing
new details

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.583
about his time in office,
thanks to what seems like

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.118
a never-ending parade
of tell-all books

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:27.487
scheduled for publication,

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.956
each filled with more
damning new details

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:32.692
about just how much
of a sociopath he was.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.927
There are so many Trump books
on the shelves

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.729
that he's bleeding
into other books.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.765
The other day, my son found him

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.200
next to Waldo.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.602
[ As Trump ]
He's right here, kid.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.136
He's right here.

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.771
And they all have titles
that make them sound

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:48.373
like straight-to-DVD
Steven Seagal movies --

00:01:48.373 --> 00:01:49.575
"Nightmare Scenario,"

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.377
"Inflection Point,"
"Tipping Point,"

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.446
"Hoax," "Rage,"
"Fear," "Fire," "Fury,"

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.781
"Fire and Fury"...

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.352
I mean, do these people
actually read these?

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:02.421
We all lived with a knot
in our belly for four years.

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:05.691
Who wants to read an 800-page
deep dive about that?

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:07.160
It'd be like reading
a book called...

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.931
Maybe they're all just
those cut-out books

00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:15.000
you can use to hide your weed
from your dog walker.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.770
Besides, don't we all just get
the craziest tidbits

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.672
cherry-picked for us on Twitter
or cable news

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.007
or from late night talk shows?
Oh, and speaking of which,

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.709
here's a cable news clip
with a tidbit

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:24.944
from a new Trump tell-all.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.345
-Stunning revelations
this morning

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.080
about the Trump
administration's response

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.482
during the early days
of the pandemic.

00:02:30.482 --> 00:02:33.052
In a new book, entitled
"Nightmare Scenario,"

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.320
Washington Post journalists

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.923
Yasmeen Abutaleb
and Damian Paletta report

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.424
how President Trump suggested

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:42.328
sending Americans with COVID-19
to Guantánamo Bay.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.430
-The book draws
on early conversations,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.432
as told by staffers
and government leaders,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.735
like this one, when White House
officials debated

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:51.404
whether to bring infected
Americans home...

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:09.689
-Only Trump would refer
to Guantánamo Bay

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.357
as "an island that we own."

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.225
It's such a reminder
that he will always,

00:03:13.225 --> 00:03:14.593
first and foremost,

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:15.895
be a real estate guy.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.564
Also, Guantánamo Bay
is not an island, you dolt.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.032
It's right there in the name.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:23.702
It's a naval base and detention
camp on the island of Cuba.

00:03:23.702 --> 00:03:25.504
An island we do not own
because --

00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:27.673
and I'm not a history buff,
but I think this is right --

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:30.075
JFK couldn't pass
the co-op board.

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:32.177
I will say,
it would've been hilarious,

00:03:32.177 --> 00:03:34.914
watching Trump try
to rebrand Guantánamo

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.883
as a fun place
for people to spend a week.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:40.153
[ As Trump ]
Welcome to Guantána-Lago
Spa &amp; Resort.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.554
Make sure you check out the bay.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.723
I heard it is full of pigs.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.390
[ Laughter ]
Also, was there like

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.926
a fantasy football draft,

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:51.097
but for the stories each staffer
got to tell for their books?

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.598
"I can't decide between the time

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.234
he wanted to send cruise ship
passengers to Gitmo

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.737
or the time he asked if he
could legally send SEAL Team Six

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.038
to rough up Lorne Michaels."

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.473
[ As Michaels ]
So, I'm up late,

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.775
[ Laughter ]
reading a first edition
Evelyn Waugh,

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.411
and I see that little red dot
on the wall

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.713
that they have
on sniper rifles

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.614
and, from that moment, I knew --

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:11.150
it's SEAL Team Six.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:14.153
The Trump era was a catastrophe
of unprecedented proportions

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.988
and, yet, Republicans
are hell-bent

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.790
on repeating it,
if they get a chance,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.492
that's why they're passing
a barrage

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.694
of voter suppression bills
that would allow them

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.329
to overturn
future election results

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.831
and why they blocked

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.765
the For the People
voting rights bill yesterday.

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:29.802
And, yet, even with that
brewing crisis on the horizon,

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:32.338
there's a small group
of Democratic senators

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:35.641
who are still super concerned
with preserving the filibuster

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:38.578
and giving Republicans a veto
over their agenda,

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.046
like Arizona
Senator Kyrsten Sinema,

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:42.949
who made some truly
ludicrous arguments

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.852
in favor of the filibuster,
in an op-ed earlier this week.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:48.054
-Kyrsten Sinema wrote
for The Washington Post.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.422
She said...

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:12.011
-Well, that's just
how democracy works.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.914
You pass laws and then,
if your opponents take power,

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.181
they can change those laws,

00:05:16.181 --> 00:05:19.185
unless you rally
public opinion to your side,

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:20.853
which is your job
as a politician.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:24.157
Didn't any of you people watch
"Schoolhouse Rock" as a kid?

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.491
Although I'm guessing,
in Sinema's case,

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.925
she watched more,

00:05:26.925 --> 00:05:29.895
I don't know,
music videos by ska bands?

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.029
She looks like she's going

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:33.966
to a Mighty Mighty Bosstones
concert in 1992.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.235
At least, that's
the impression that I get.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:37.303
[ Knock-knock, chuckle ]

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.672
Your job is to make progress

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.740
and then fight
to protect that progress

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.409
by galvanizing popular support.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.945
You can't just resign yourself
to doing nothing

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.847
because Republicans
might eventually

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.281
undo whatever bill you pass.

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:50.850
For one thing,
that's not a given.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.618
Republicans couldn't get rid
of Obamacare,

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:53.986
even with a simple majority,

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.389
because it was super popular
and people were outraged.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.391
Also, Republicans
don't seem to care

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.892
if they get support
from Democrats.

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.094
In fact, they're doing
the opposite.

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:02.761
Across the country,
they're passing

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:05.063
voter suppression bills
on party line votes.

00:06:05.063 --> 00:06:06.632
-I followed all
of these debates.

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:09.768
They were party line,
simple majority debates

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:11.537
in Georgia, in Arizona...

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:14.106
-Yes, sir.
-...in Florida,
in all of these states,

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:15.174
making it harder to vote.

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.775
And Republicans didn't say, "Oh,

00:06:16.775 --> 00:06:18.344
what will the Democrats say
about us?

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.545
We need bipartisanship."
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:22.014
-The entire point
of voter suppression is

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:24.716
to make it harder for your
opponents to be able to vote.

00:06:24.716 --> 00:06:26.585
And so there's just
two standards here.

00:06:26.585 --> 00:06:30.089
There's the game being played
by Republicans in the states,

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.725
where they do whatever they can
to undermine democracy.

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:33.826
Then, there's the game
being played

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.528
by Democrats in Washington,

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:38.430
where they fail to protect
American democracy

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.466
because of these arcane rules

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.702
that nobody actually
cares about.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:45.370
In 100 years, nobody's going
to care about the filibuster,

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:47.873
if the right to vote
is undermined for decades.

00:06:47.873 --> 00:06:50.343
-He's right. No one gives
a [bleep] about the filibuster.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.278
Most people don't even know
where it came from,

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:54.380
why it exists,
why it's called a filibuster,

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.648
or where that word
even came from.

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:58.650
True story --
it's a Dutch word, vribuyter,

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.553
which translates
to "freebooter,"

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.287
and was used to mean "pirate."

00:07:02.287 --> 00:07:04.223
So, by respecting
the filibuster,

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.791
we're loosely
supporting pirates,

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:07.092
which makes sense,
because, basically,

00:07:07.092 --> 00:07:08.895
Mitch McConnell's entire career
has been him

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:11.130
boarding the SS Democracy
and saying --

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.599
[ As McConnell ]
Uh, I'm the captain now.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:14.600
[ Laughter ]
Too long a walk to get

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.302
to the McConnell impression?

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.770
Just long enough?
I hope it was worth it

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.039
because it's a real strain
on my vocal cords.

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:23.141
Not the part just now,
the hours of vocal warm-ups.

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:24.576
[ As McConnell ]
Red leather, yellow leather.

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:25.811
Red leather,
yellow leather.

00:07:25.811 --> 00:07:28.147
The jolly collie
swallowed a lollipop.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:29.982
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:32.251
Anyway, no one cares
about the filibuster,

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:34.553
and Democrats,
like Sinema and Joe Manchin,

00:07:34.553 --> 00:07:35.921
need to stop playing

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:38.491
by different self-imposed rules
than Republicans.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:41.293
When Trump supporters were
scaling the walls of the Capitol

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:42.928
to overthrow the government,
they weren't like,

00:07:42.928 --> 00:07:44.797
"Aw, man, I hope the Democrats
are cool with this.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:45.865
Should we have invited
some of them?

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.800
You know, just for optics?"

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.035
The difference
with Republicans

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:50.036
is so infuriating.

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:51.236
Democrats are worried that,

00:07:51.236 --> 00:07:52.505
if they lose the next election,

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:54.106
their legislation
could get overturned,

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.407
while Republicans
are still trying

00:07:55.407 --> 00:07:56.909
to overturn the last election.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:59.945
In Arizona, the sham election
audit has gotten so insane,

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:02.415
they're hunting for bamboo
ballots and secret watermarks

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:04.416
and sending copies
of voting data

00:08:04.416 --> 00:08:07.954
to a mysterious laboratory
in a remote location in Montana.

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:09.288
-On this piece of property,

00:08:09.288 --> 00:08:11.090
in a remote part of Montana,

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.691
people may, at this very minute,

00:08:12.691 --> 00:08:15.961
be analyzing voting data
from the state of Arizona,

00:08:15.961 --> 00:08:18.264
as part of the so-called
Arizona audit.

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:20.632
So, as you might expect,
we're left wondering where,

00:08:20.632 --> 00:08:22.267
in the state of Montana,

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:25.137
are the copies of this
voting data being analyzed?

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:27.406
Where is the "secure,
powerful lab"?

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:29.742
So could the information
be here?

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:31.243
We could tell you,
as we walk up here,

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:33.479
the first thing you see on this
big piece of land is the sign --

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:34.780
"Private property.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.782
Trespassing for any purpose
is strictly forbidden.

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:38.550
Violators will be prosecuted."

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.253
We can't cross this area.

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:42.221
We can show you, though,
from this area,

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:45.224
what looks like a cabin
on this property.

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:48.093
Is this the "secure,
powerful laboratory"?

00:08:48.093 --> 00:08:51.830
Is Arizona voting data
inside that cabin?

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:52.932
We just don't know.

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:54.166
But it could be.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.935
-Dude, be careful on the side
of the highway,

00:08:55.935 --> 00:08:57.770
or people are going to think
you're a hitchhiker.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.306
"Anderson, I'm currently
in a windowless white van

00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:02.140
with a man named Rex, who says

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.809
I can crash with him
for the night

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:05.811
and have all
the ice cream I want,

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:08.447
as long as I make a sacrifice
of fresh deer meat

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:11.183
to the wood spirit Galfgamar.

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:12.351
Back to you, Anderson."

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:13.819
That's how insane
things are right now.

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:15.754
CNN reporters are hunting
for voting data

00:09:15.754 --> 00:09:17.423
on the side of a highway
three states away

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:20.025
because Republicans shifted
to a secret location

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:22.094
in the middle of nowhere,
with no outside observers,

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:23.429
in the name
of election integrity.

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:25.831
This is all starting to sound
like a storyline

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.299
from the next season of "Ozark,"

00:09:27.299 --> 00:09:29.134
which, thanks
to his Netflix deal,

00:09:29.134 --> 00:09:30.302
stars Barack Obama.

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:32.405
[ As Obama ]
Uh....Laura.

00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:34.306
We got to find the ballots,

00:09:34.306 --> 00:09:36.075
or the cartel will, uh,

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:37.209
come after us.

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:39.045
"Uh, sir, her character's
name is Wendy."

00:09:39.045 --> 00:09:40.779
Well, let's dub it in later.

00:09:40.779 --> 00:09:43.315
ADR it!

00:09:43.315 --> 00:09:45.551
I'm in a groove.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:47.920
Every day, we find out more
about just how much

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.488
of a nightmare
the Trump era was

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:51.223
and, every day,
Republicans do whatever they can

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:53.192
to force that nightmare
on us again.

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:54.693
They're passing bills
across the country,

00:09:54.693 --> 00:09:57.096
making it easier to overturn
the next election,

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:59.932
and sending voting data
to mysterious locations

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:01.300
to overturn the last election.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.136
The guessing game about where
Arizona Republicans sent

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:06.205
all that voting data
is getting so crazy,

00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:07.572
eventually,
we're going to have to ask...

00:10:07.572 --> 00:10:09.241
-"What about Guantánamo?"

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.809
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:10.809 --> 00:10:14.580
♪♪

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.081
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:10:16.081 --> 00:10:17.382
over two million meals a year

00:10:17.382 --> 00:10:19.885
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:21.653
cancer, and other
serious illnesses

00:10:21.653 --> 00:10:23.655
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:10:23.655 --> 00:10:26.358
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:10:26.358 --> 00:10:29.595
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

